Wake up, the water is strangling you again.

In the hotel shower you tried drowning yourself. 
But you turned your back on death and the water 
christened you. 

Why are you lying on your bed, 
a radio taken apart 
to find the voice inside its head?

You've spent days living as a ghost,
release the human behind your teeth.

What is your name? Where were you born? 
None of that matters. Time is not a morgue.

A bird with wet wings sings 
to the cold moon after the storm.

What is the name you'll christen yourself?

